{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"7b344c44f58b45d91fb36753b34a5c49ee5d62aeae10045c0f4dae96a0370778","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_d6cb2679e6169f091f8eb2bcd4575b0508dc1386884ff5ce82ca4f6ad40cf0fa","overall_assessment":"The paper is a theoretical contribution with standard data usage practices. The primary policy concern is the violation of double-blind anonymity due to the presence of author names, affiliations, and emails in the provided text. Additionally, the lack of a broader impact statement is a minor compliance gap for modern conference standards.","paper_id":"B1mAJI9gl","paper_identity_sha256":"415000ee81ced564dece09ccd5c076b91893a86d3d70389f2ad39c6e7f11eef5","prompt_identity_sha256":"f9fa75600486f65079d65824c94325ed9be65e40ca635b5ee5211f67eec874a4","raw_response_sha256":"8be619e2e9722192cf5ec50cc545717ba0a620f9cfc80856a419cadf607abea5","request_identity_sha256":"a8d82afc61e0f227d5f354b732db90c04bb682d112d44fdc2af59c37ec1d9932","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper focuses on the theoretical analysis of CNN invertibility and does not explicitly discuss ethical risks, fairness, bias, or potential harms to marginalized populations. As a theoretical work on signal recovery and network properties, direct ethical implications are minimal, but the lack of a broader impact statement or discussion on responsible AI practices is noted. The use of standard datasets like CIFAR-10 and ImageNet for validation is standard practice, but no specific ethical review or mitigation strategies for potential misuse of invertibility techniques (e.g., privacy leakage via reconstruction) are provided.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes standard public datasets, specifically CIFAR-10 and the ILSVRC-2012 (ImageNet) validation set, for empirical validation. These datasets are widely used in the machine learning community and are generally considered to have appropriate licensing for research purposes. The paper does not involve the collection of new personal data or sensitive information. The use of pretrained VGGNet filters is consistent with standard academic practice. No specific privacy violations or consent issues are apparent from the text, as the data used is non-personal and publicly available.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The provided paper text includes full author names (Anna C. Gilbert, Yi Zhang, Kibok Lee, Yuting Zhang, Honglak Lee) and institutional affiliations (University of Michigan, Google Brain) on the title page. Additionally, email addresses are listed. For a double-blind review venue like ICLR, this constitutes a violation of anonymity policies unless the submission was explicitly exempted or the review process is single-blind. The presence of these identifiers allows for the identification of the authors and their affiliations, which compromises the double-blind review process.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-005","SRC-018"],"review_text":"The paper cites relevant prior work extensively, including Arora et al., Dosovitskiy and Brox, Zhao et al., Bruna et al., and Zhang et al., indicating proper attribution of related ideas. The mathematical framework and specific empirical results appear to be original contributions. There is no evidence of plagiarism or dual submission within the provided text. The use of standard algorithms like IHT and model-based compressive sensing is properly cited to their original sources (Blumensath and Davies, Baraniuk et al.).","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated 'Broader Impact' section or a checklist for societal considerations, which are increasingly required or recommended at venues like ICLR. While the work is primarily theoretical, the ability to invert CNNs has potential implications for privacy (e.g., reconstructing inputs from hidden states) and security. The absence of a discussion on these broader societal impacts, as well as the lack of explicit software/data license statements for any released code or data, represents a gap in compliance with modern broader impact reporting standards.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"6987098e46ea28bc842223252bf2e0798af9c546dd082a8904cf763feece96f9","paper_id":"B1mAJI9gl","paper_ordinal":14,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"8be619e2e9722192cf5ec50cc545717ba0a620f9cfc80856a419cadf607abea5","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1mAJI9gl","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"58682fe41c34b9becdb68f55f8390664d45f36f31e0fc26df0cc994d95377806","request_identity_sha256":"a8d82afc61e0f227d5f354b732db90c04bb682d112d44fdc2af59c37ec1d9932","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":890,"prompt_tokens":18849,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19739},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"a8d82afc61e0f227d5f354b732db90c04bb682d112d44fdc2af59c37ec1d9932","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}